From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 21:23:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: mediatek: mt6797: describe the CPU PMU

perf has only software events on MT6797 because the SoC DT has no PMU
node, so the ARMv8 PMU driver never probes.

All ten cores, the eight Cortex-A53s and the two Cortex-A72s, signal
their PMU overflow on PPI 7 (INTID 23), active low, the same per-CPU
interrupt the vendor kernel uses. One PPI cannot be split between two
CPU types here without GIC PPI partitions, so describe a single generic
"arm,armv8-pmuv3" PMU that covers every CPU. The architected events,
such as cycles and instructions, have the same numbers on both cores.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797.dtsi | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797.dtsi
index 94884ab..98bd5bd 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/mediatek/mt6797.dtsi
@@ -249,6 +249,13 @@
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 	};
+
+	pmu {
+		compatible = "arm,armv8-pmuv3";
+		interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
+		interrupts = <GIC_PPI 7 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>;
+	};
+
 	timer {
 		compatible = "arm,armv8-timer";
 		interrupt-parent = <&gic>;
